e":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I added the \"Divide Curve Stats\" component and `dotnet build` succeeds with 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n\nThe new code is in `GeometryPack.cs`. It follows the existing `Collection.cs` pattern: an `IGeometryPack` interface carries `[GrasshopperCollection(\"Bench\", \"Geometry\")]`, and `GeometryPack` implements it. I kept it in its own file because the subcategory is new.\n\nThe method takes `Curve curve` and `int count` (default 10). It returns `(List<Point3d> Points, double Length)`.\n\nChoices I made:\n- **Point count:** Points includes both endpoints, so Count = 10 gives 10 segments and 11 points. If you want only the 10 interior division points, change `includeEnds` to `false` in `GeometryPack.cs`.\n- **Equal length:** the division uses curve parameters from `DivideByCount`, which are spaced at equal arc length. Each parameter is then converted to a point with `PointAt`.\n- **Errors:** a null curve or a Count below 1 throws, which shows an error in Grasshopper. A failed division also throws.\n\nI only checked that it compiles. I did not run it inside Grasshopper. The post-build step copies the DLL to `%AppData%\\Grasshopper\\Libraries\\Betta\\`, so loading the new build there is the next check.","ttft_ms":2487,"type":"result","duration_ms":41069,"uuid":"5943975a-1fad-44a3-9e6a-5daebe6dc3e0","ttft_stream_ms":2326,"time_to_request_ms":720,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":164,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":68,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":1,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":210,"init_frame_send":13,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":44,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":3,"autocompact":5,"request_announcements":29,"query_setup":2,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":94,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":24,"request_build":22},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_